syllabai-parser repo. What is it's purpose

Within the SyllabAI ecosystem, syllabai-parser serves as the content transformation and extraction bridge that turns raw, unstructured examination materials (PDFs and OCR outputs) into structured, queryable data for the rest of the platform.

Here is its specific role and purpose across the architecture:

1. The Core Problem It Solves
Official past papers (Question Papers, Mark Schemes, Examiner Reports) exist as static, multi-column PDFs containing complex formatting—chemical equations, tables, sub-questions (e.g., 1(a)(i)), and embedded diagram figures.

The backend (syllabai-core) and frontend (syllabai-web) cannot directly consume raw PDFs. syllabai-parser sits between raw documents and the application layer to parse, extract, and clean this content into standardized data structures.

2. Main Responsibilities & Pipeline Functions
GLM-OCR Integration & Normalization (GLM_OCR_CONTENT.md):

Consumes OCR outputs generated by Z.ai GLM-OCR and processes them into structured Markdown.

Preserves the alignment between questions and their corresponding diagrams/assets.

Granular Decomposition (Questions & Sub-parts):

Breaks monolithic exam papers down into atomic units: Question and QuestionPart entities.

Isolates mark schemes, maximum marks available, method/accuracy marks (M/A marks), and examiner notes per sub-part.

The OCR-to-Core Bridge Contract (t-c02-bridge-contract):

Enforces an invariant contract between python-based parser scripts and the Java backend (syllabai-core).

Ensures that downstream services (like the Knapsack Exam Generator or the RAG chatbot) receive deterministic JSON/Markdown schemas rather than depending on local filesystem paths or ad-hoc file names.

Asset & Image Reference Preservation:

Extracts embedded visual diagrams, graphs, and apparatus setups, ensuring each question part maintains a permanent reference to its visual assets (which later get archived to Cloudflare R2 storage).

3. Position in the Multi-Repo Architecture
[syllabai-pastpapers] (Raw PDFs & Scraping Ledgers)
         │
         ▼
[syllabai-parser]     <-- GLM-OCR parsing, atomization into Question/Part, image asset recovery
         │
         ▼
[syllabai-core]       <-- Spring Boot monolith (ingests structured JSON, populates Postgres/pgvector)
         │
         ▼
[syllabai-web]        <-- Next.js client renders questions via stable Question API
In short: syllabai-parser is the ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) engine of the project—it converts messy, human-readable exam papers into machine-actionable assessment items that power the Knowledge Graph and RAG pipelines.

