In an exam paper, Question 3(b) often references a diagram of a fractional distillation column sitting on page 4. Standard loaders extract the image as an unlinked raw binary dump. VLMs like GLM-OCR preserve the context by outputting an image tag right inside the markdown stream where the question references it.

